message.content:
Here’s how you can invoke the helper that appends the node‑ID to your `StringBuilder`.  
Just pass the `LogEvent` instance and the `StringBuilder` instance to the function – the tool will take care of converting them to the underlying Java objects.

```java
// Assume you already have a LogEvent instance called logEvent
// and a StringBuilder that you want to append to.
StringBuilder logBuilder = new StringBuilder();

// Call the helper – it will append the node ID (if present) to logBuilder.
functions.NodeIdConverter_format({
    event: logEvent,          // the LogEvent that contains the node ID
    toAppendTo: logBuilder    // the StringBuilder to which the node ID will be appended
});
```

After this call, `logBuilder` will contain the original content plus the node ID (if it was available in the `LogEvent`).

